#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:649
msgid ""
"The subject expression ``subject_expr`` is evaluated and a resulting subject"
" value obtained. If the subject expression contains a comma, a tuple is "
"constructed using :ref:`the standard rules <typesseq-tuple>`."
msgstr ""
"Výraz subjektu ``subject_expr`` se vyhodnotí a získá se výsledná hodnota "
"subjektu. Pokud výraz subjektu obsahuje čárku, vytvoří se n-tice podle "
":ref:`standardních pravidel <typesseq-tuple>`."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:653
msgid ""
"Each pattern in a ``case_block`` is attempted to match with the subject "
"value. The specific rules for success or failure are described below. The "
"match attempt can also bind some or all of the standalone names within the "
"pattern. The precise pattern binding rules vary per pattern type and are "
"specified below.  **Name bindings made during a successful pattern match "
"outlive the executed block and can be used after the match statement**."
msgstr ""
"Každý vzorek v ``case_block`` se pokusí matchovat s hodnotou subjektu. "
"Specifická pravidla pro úspěch nebo neúspěch jsou popsána níže. Pokus o "
"match může také vyvázat některá nebo všechna samostatná jména v rámci "
"vzorců. Přesná pravidla vazby vzorců se liší podle typu vzorců a jsou "
"specifikována níže. **Vázání jmen během úspěšné shody vzorců přežije "
"spustený blok a mohou se používat po příkazu match**."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:662
msgid ""
"During failed pattern matches, some subpatterns may succeed.  Do not rely on"
" bindings being made for a failed match.  Conversely, do not rely on "
"variables remaining unchanged after a failed match.  The exact behavior is "
"dependent on implementation and may vary.  This is an intentional decision "
"made to allow different implementations to add optimizations."
msgstr ""
"Během neúspěšných shod vzorců mohou některé podvzorky uspokojit. Nespo "
"léhajte na tom, že se važby uskutečňují pro neúspěšné shody. Naopak, "
"nespolejte na tom, že proměnné zůstanout nezměněny ch po neúspěšné shodě. "
"Přesné chování závisí na implementaci a může se lišit. Toto je úmýslné "
"rozhodnutí učiněné tak, aby dovolilo různým implementacím přidat "
"optimalizace."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:669
msgid ""
"If the pattern succeeds, the corresponding guard (if present) is evaluated. "
"In this case all name bindings are guaranteed to have happened."
msgstr ""
"Pokud vzorek uspokojit, vyhodnotí se odpovídající stáž (pokud je přítomna). "
"V tomto případě jsou všechna vázání jmen zaručena, že k nim došlo."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:672
msgid ""
"If the guard evaluates as true or is missing, the ``block`` inside "
"``case_block`` is executed."
msgstr ""
"Pokud stáž vyhodnotí jako pravdivá nebo chybí, provede se ``block`` uvnitř "
"``case_block``."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:675
msgid "Otherwise, the next ``case_block`` is attempted as described above."
msgstr ""
"V opačném případě se pokusí následující ``case_block``, jak je popsáno výše."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:677
msgid "If there are no further case blocks, the match statement is completed."
msgstr "Pokud nejsou další bloky case, příkaz match je dokončen."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:681
msgid ""
"Users should generally never rely on a pattern being evaluated.  Depending "
"on implementation, the interpreter may cache values or use other "
"optimizations which skip repeated evaluations."
msgstr ""
"Uživatelé by měli obecně nikdy nespolejat na tom, že se vzorek vyhodnocuje. "
"V závislosti na implementaci má interpretátor může ukládat hodnoty nebo "
"používat jiné optimalizace, které přeskočí opakované vyhodnocování."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:685
msgid "A sample match statement::"
msgstr "Ukázka příkazu match::"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:687
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> flag = False\n"
">>> match (100, 200):\n"
"...    case (100, 300):  # Mismatch: 200 != 300\n"
"...        print('Case 1')\n"
"...    case (100, 200) if flag:  # Successful match, but guard fails\n"
"...        print('Case 2')\n"
"...    case (100, y):  # Matches and binds y to 200\n"
"...        print(f'Case 3, y: {y}')\n"
"...    case _:  # Pattern not attempted\n"
"...        print('Case 4, I match anything!')\n"
"...\n"
"Case 3, y: 200"
msgstr ""
">>> flag = False\n"
">>> match (100, 200):\n"
"...    case (100, 300):  # Neshoda: 200 != 300\n"
"...        print('Case 1')\n"
"...    case (100, 200) if flag:  # Úspěšná shoda, ale stáž selhává\n"
"...        print('Case 2')\n"
"...    case (100, y):  # Matchuje a váže y na 200\n"
"...        print(f'Case 3, y: {y}')\n"
"...    case _:  # Vzorek se nepokouší\n"
"...        print('Case 4, I match anything!')\n"
"...\n"
"Case 3, y: 200"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:701
msgid ""
"In this case, ``if flag`` is a guard.  Read more about that in the next "
"section."
msgstr ""
"V tomto případě je ``if flag`` stáž. Přečtněte si více o tom v následující "
"části."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:704
msgid "Guards"
msgstr "Stáže"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:711
msgid ""
"A ``guard`` (which is part of the ``case``) must succeed for code inside the"
" ``case`` block to execute.  It takes the form: :keyword:`if` followed by an"
" expression."
msgstr ""
"``Guard`` (která je částí ``case``) musí uspokojit, aby se kód uvnitř bloku "
"``case`` spustil. Obsahuje formu: :keyword:`if` následováno výrazu."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:716
msgid "The logical flow of a ``case`` block with a ``guard`` follows:"
msgstr "Logický tok bloku ``case`` se ``guard`` následuje:"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:718
msgid ""
"Check that the pattern in the ``case`` block succeeded.  If the pattern "
"failed, the ``guard`` is not evaluated and the next ``case`` block is "
"checked."
msgstr ""
"Zkontrolujte, že se vzorek v bloku ``case`` podařil. Pokud se vzorek "
"nepovedl, ``guard`` se nevyhodnocuje a kontroluje se následující blok "
"``case``."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:722
msgid "If the pattern succeeded, evaluate the ``guard``."
msgstr "Pokud se vzorek podařil, vyhodnoťte ``guard``."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:724
msgid ""
"If the ``guard`` condition evaluates as true, the case block is selected."
msgstr ""
"Pokud se podminka ``guard`` vyhodnotí jako pravdivá, vybere se blok case."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:727
msgid ""
"If the ``guard`` condition evaluates as false, the case block is not "
"selected."
msgstr ""
"Pokud se podminka ``guard`` vyhodnotí jako nepravdivá, blok case se "
"nevybere."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:730
msgid ""
"If the ``guard`` raises an exception during evaluation, the exception "
"bubbles up."
msgstr ""
"Pokud ``guard`` vyvolá výjimku během vyhodnocování, výjimka se rozmří."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:733
msgid ""
"Guards are allowed to have side effects as they are expressions.  Guard "
"evaluation must proceed from the first to the last case block, one at a "
"time, skipping case blocks whose pattern(s) don't all succeed. (I.e., guard "
"evaluation must happen in order.) Guard evaluation must stop once a case "
"block is selected."
msgstr ""
"Stáže mohou mít vedlejší činky, protože jsou výrazy. Vyhodnocování stáž musí"
" probíhat od prvního po poslední blok case, jeden po druhém, přeskočím bloky"
" case, jejichž vzorek(y) nejsou všechny úspěšné. (To znamená, že "
"vyhodnocování stáž musí probíhat v pořadí.) Vyhodnocování stáž musí skončit,"
" jakmile se vybere blok case."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:743
msgid "Irrefutable Case Blocks"
msgstr "Nezačínatelné bloky Case"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:747
msgid ""
"An irrefutable case block is a match-all case block.  A match statement may "
"have at most one irrefutable case block, and it must be last."
msgstr ""
"Nezačínatelný blok case je blok match-all. Příkaz match může mít nejvýše "
"jeden nezačínatelný blok case a musí být poslední."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:750
msgid ""
"A case block is considered irrefutable if it has no guard and its pattern is"
" irrefutable.  A pattern is considered irrefutable if we can prove from its "
"syntax alone that it will always succeed.  Only the following patterns are "
"irrefutable:"
msgstr ""
"Blok case se považuje za nezačínatelný, pokud nemá stáž a jeho vzorek je "
"nezačínatelný. Vzorek se považuje za nezačínatelný, pokud můžeme z jeho "
"syntaxe samoté dokázat, že vždy uspokojit. Pouze následující vzorek jsou "
"nezačínatelné:"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:755
msgid ":ref:`as-patterns` whose left-hand side is irrefutable"
msgstr ":ref:`as-patterns` jejichž levá strana je nezačínatelná"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:757
msgid ":ref:`or-patterns` containing at least one irrefutable pattern"
msgstr ":ref:`or-patterns` obsahující alespoň jeden nezačínatelný vzorek"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:759
msgid ":ref:`capture-patterns`"
msgstr ":ref:`capture-patterns`"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:761
msgid ":ref:`wildcard-patterns`"
msgstr ":ref:`wildcard-patterns`"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:763
msgid "parenthesized irrefutable patterns"
msgstr "vároze závork nénezačínatelné vzorek"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:767
msgid "Patterns"
msgstr "Vzorek"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:774
msgid "This section uses grammar notations beyond standard EBNF:"
msgstr "Tato část používá grmatické notace mimo standardní EBNF:"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:776
msgid "the notation ``SEP.RULE+`` is shorthand for ``RULE (SEP RULE)*``"
msgstr "znaení ``SEP.RULE+`` je zkráceným způsobem pro ``RULE (SEP RULE)*``"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:778
msgid "the notation ``!RULE`` is shorthand for a negative lookahead assertion"
msgstr "notace ``!RULE`` je zkrácenkou pro výrazu negativného lookahead"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:781
msgid "The top-level syntax for ``patterns`` is:"
msgstr "Syntaxe nejvysší úrovně pro ``patterns`` je:"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:795
msgid ""
"The descriptions below will include a description \"in simple terms\" of "
"what a pattern does for illustration purposes (credits to Raymond Hettinger "
"for a document that inspired most of the descriptions). Note that these "
"descriptions are purely for illustration purposes and **may not** reflect "
"the underlying implementation.  Furthermore, they do not cover all valid "
"forms."
msgstr ""
"Popisy níže budou obsahovat popis \"jednoduchy mi slovy\" toho, co vzorek "
"dělá pro ilustrační účely (vědy Ray Hetlingeru za dokument, který inspiroval"
" většinu popisů). Poznámka, že tyto popisy jsou čistě pro ilustrační účely a"
" **nemusí** odrážet podkladové implementace. Napříd, nejsou pokryty všemi "
"platnými formami."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:805
msgid "OR Patterns"
msgstr "NEBO Vzorek"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:807
msgid ""
"An OR pattern is two or more patterns separated by vertical bars ``|``.  "
"Syntax:"
msgstr ""
"Vzorek OR jsou dva nebo více vzorců oddělených svislým pruhem ``|``. Syntax:"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:813
msgid ""
"Only the final subpattern may be :ref:`irrefutable <irrefutable_case>`, and "
"each subpattern must bind the same set of names to avoid ambiguity."
msgstr ""
"Pouze poslední podvzorek má být :ref:`nezačínatelný <irrefutable_case>` a "
"každý podvzorek musí vazat stejné sady jmen, aby se vyhnul nejasnosti."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:816
msgid ""
"An OR pattern matches each of its subpatterns in turn to the subject value, "
"until one succeeds.  The OR pattern is then considered successful.  "
"Otherwise, if none of the subpatterns succeed, the OR pattern fails."
msgstr ""
"Vzorek OR matchuje každý ze svých podvzorců postupně proti hodnotě subjektu,"
" dokud jeden neuspokojit. Vzorek OR se pak považuje za úspěšný. V opačném "
"případě, pokud žádný z podvzorců neuspokojit, vzorek OR selhává."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:820
msgid ""
"In simple terms, ``P1 | P2 | ...`` will try to match ``P1``, if it fails it "
"will try to match ``P2``, succeeding immediately if any succeeds, failing "
"otherwise."
msgstr ""
"Jednoduchy mi slovy ``P1 | P2 | ...`` se pokusí matchovat ``P1``, pokud "
"selhává, pokusí se matchovat ``P2``, ihned uspokojit, pokud něco uspokojit, "
"jinak selhává."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:826
msgid "AS Patterns"
msgstr "JAKO Vzorek"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:828
msgid ""
"An AS pattern matches an OR pattern on the left of the :keyword:`as` keyword"
" against a subject.  Syntax:"
msgstr ""
"Vzorek AS matchuje vzorek OR vlevo klavesu :keyword:`as` proti subjektu. "
"Syntax:"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:834
msgid ""
"If the OR pattern fails, the AS pattern fails.  Otherwise, the AS pattern "
"binds the subject to the name on the right of the as keyword and succeeds. "
"``capture_pattern`` cannot be a ``_``."
msgstr ""
"Pokud vzorek OR selhává, vzorek AS selhává. V opačném případě vzorek AS váže"
" subjekt k jménu napravo od klavesu as a uspokojit. ``capture_pattern`` "
"nemůže být ``_``."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:838
msgid ""
"In simple terms ``P as NAME`` will match with ``P``, and on success it will "
"set ``NAME = <subject>``."
msgstr ""
"Jednoduchy mi slovy ``P as NAME`` se pokusí matchovat s ``P`` a při úspěchu "
"nastaví ``NAME = <subject>``."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:845
msgid "Literal Patterns"
msgstr "Literalní vzorek"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:847
msgid ""
"A literal pattern corresponds to most :ref:`literals <literals>` in Python."
"  Syntax:"
msgstr ""
"Literalní vzorek odpovídá většině :ref:`literálů <literals>` v Pythonu. "
"Syntax:"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:860
msgid ""
"The rule ``strings`` and the token ``NUMBER`` are defined in the "
":doc:`standard Python grammar <./grammar>`.  Triple-quoted strings are "
"supported.  Raw strings and byte strings are supported.  :ref:`f-strings` "
"and :ref:`t-strings` are not supported."
msgstr ""
"Pravidlo ``strings`` a token ``NUMBER`` jsou definovány v :doc:`standardní "
"gramatice Python <./grammar>`. Trojíté citáty jsou podporovány. Surové "
"řetězce a bajty jsou podporovány. :ref:`f-strings` a :ref:`t-strings` nejsou"
" podporovány."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:865
msgid ""
"The forms ``signed_number '+' NUMBER`` and ``signed_number '-' NUMBER`` are "
"for expressing :ref:`complex numbers <imaginary>`; they require a real "
"number on the left and an imaginary number on the right. E.g. ``3 + 4j``."
msgstr ""
"Formy ``signed_number '+' NUMBER`` a ``signed_number '-' NUMBER`` jsou pro "
"vyjádření :ref:`komplexních čísel <imaginary>`; vyžadují reálné číslo vlevo "
"a imaginární číslo vpravo. Např. ``3 + 4j``."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:869
msgid ""
"In simple terms, ``LITERAL`` will succeed only if ``<subject> == LITERAL``. "
"For the singletons ``None``, ``True`` and ``False``, the :keyword:`is` "
"operator is used."
msgstr ""
"Jednoduchy mi slovy, ``LITERAL`` bude úspěšný pouze pokud ``<subject> == "
"LITERAL``. Pro singletony ``None``, ``True`` a ``False`` se používá operátor"
" :keyword:`is`."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:875
msgid "Capture Patterns"
msgstr "Zachycení vzorců"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:877
msgid "A capture pattern binds the subject value to a name. Syntax:"
msgstr "Vzorek pro zachycení váže hodnotu subjektu k jménu. Syntax:"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:883
msgid ""
"A single underscore ``_`` is not a capture pattern (this is what ``!'_'`` "
"expresses). It is instead treated as a :token:`~python-"
"grammar:wildcard_pattern`."
msgstr ""
"Jedna pomlčka ``_`` není vzorek pro zachycení (toto je co vyjadřuje "
"``!'_'``). Zaměštěčuje se to jako :token:`~python-grammar:wildcard_pattern`."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:887
msgid ""
"In a given pattern, a given name can only be bound once.  E.g. ``case x, x: "
"...`` is invalid while ``case [x] | x: ...`` is allowed."
msgstr ""
"V daném vzorcí lze dané jméno vázat pouze jednou. Např. ``case x, x: ...`` "
"je neplatný, zatímco ``case [x] | x: ...`` je povolen."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:890
msgid ""
"Capture patterns always succeed.  The binding follows scoping rules "
"established by the assignment expression operator in :pep:`572`; the name "
"becomes a local variable in the closest containing function scope unless "
"there's an applicable :keyword:`global` or :keyword:`nonlocal` statement."
msgstr ""
"Vzorek pro zachycení vždy uspokojit. Vázání následuje pravidla rozsahu "
"zahnřzáná operátorem výrazu přiřazení v :pep:`572`; jméno se stává lokální "
"proměnné v nejblížě se obsahujícím rozsahu funkce, pokud nejsou platné "
":keyword:`global` nebo :keyword:`nonlocal` příkazy."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:895
msgid ""
"In simple terms ``NAME`` will always succeed and it will set ``NAME = "
"<subject>``."
msgstr ""
"Jednoduchy mi slovy ``NAME`` vždy uspokojit a nastaví ``NAME = <subject>``."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:900
msgid "Wildcard Patterns"
msgstr "Zástupné vzorek"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:902
msgid ""
"A wildcard pattern always succeeds (matches anything) and binds no name.  "
"Syntax:"
msgstr ""
"Zástupný vzorek vždy uspokojit (matchuje cokoli) a váže žádné jméno. Syntax:"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:908
msgid ""
"``_`` is a :ref:`soft keyword <soft-keywords>` within any pattern, but only "
"within patterns.  It is an identifier, as usual, even within ``match`` "
"subject expressions, ``guard``\\ s, and ``case`` blocks."
msgstr ""
"``_`` je :ref:`soft keyword <soft-keywords>` v rámci jakéhokoliv vzorců, ale"
" pouze v rámci vzorců. Je to identifikátor, jak je bĞžné, i v rámci "
"``match`` výrazů subjektu, ``guard``\\ s, a ``case`` bloků."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:912
msgid "In simple terms, ``_`` will always succeed."
msgstr "Jednoduchy mi slovy, ``_`` vždy uspokojit."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:917
msgid "Value Patterns"
msgstr "Vzorek hodnoty"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:919
msgid "A value pattern represents a named value in Python. Syntax:"
msgstr "Vzorek hodnoty představuje pojmenovanou hodnotu v Pythonu. Syntax:"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:927
msgid ""
"The dotted name in the pattern is looked up using standard Python :ref:`name"
" resolution rules <resolve_names>`.  The pattern succeeds if the value found"
" compares equal to the subject value (using the ``==`` equality operator)."
msgstr ""
"Tečka v nzvu v vzorcí se vyhledává podle standardních Python :ref:`pravidel "
"pro rozlišení jmen <resolve_names>`. Vzorek uspokojit, pokud se hodnota "
"nalezená rovná s hodnotou subjektu (pomocí operátoru ``==`` rovnosti)."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:932
msgid ""
"In simple terms ``NAME1.NAME2`` will succeed only if ``<subject> == "
"NAME1.NAME2``"
msgstr ""
"Jednoduchy mi slovy ``NAME1.NAME2`` bude úspěšný pouze pokud ``<subject> == "
"NAME1.NAME2``"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:936
msgid ""
"If the same value occurs multiple times in the same match statement, the "
"interpreter may cache the first value found and reuse it rather than repeat "
"the same lookup.  This cache is strictly tied to a given execution of a "
"given match statement."
msgstr ""
"Pokud se stejna hodnota objevuje vicekrat v temze prikazu match, ma "
"interpret má moznost pouzit cache prve nalezene hodnoty a zpetne ji pouzit "
"nez opakovat stejne vyhledavani. Toto cache je prisne svazano s danym "
"provedenm danem prikazu match."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:944
msgid "Group Patterns"
msgstr "Skupinove vzorek"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:946
msgid ""
"A group pattern allows users to add parentheses around patterns to emphasize"
" the intended grouping.  Otherwise, it has no additional syntax. Syntax:"
msgstr ""
"Skupinovy vzorek umoznjuje uzivatelm pridat zavorky kolem vzorc, aby "
"zduraznily zamleslene seskupeni. V opacnem pripade nema dalsi syntaxi. "
"Syntax:"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:953
msgid "In simple terms ``(P)`` has the same effect as ``P``."
msgstr "Jednoduchy mi slovy (P) ma stejny ucinek jako P."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:958
msgid "Sequence Patterns"
msgstr "Vzorek posloupnosti"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:960
msgid ""
"A sequence pattern contains several subpatterns to be matched against "
"sequence elements. The syntax is similar to the unpacking of a list or "
"tuple."
msgstr ""
"Vzorek posloupnosti obsahuje nkolik podvzorc, ktere maji byt matchovany "
"proti prvkm posloupnosti. Syntax je podobna rozbalovani seznamu nebo n-tice."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:971
msgid ""
"There is no difference if parentheses  or square brackets are used for "
"sequence patterns (i.e. ``(...)`` vs ``[...]`` )."
msgstr ""
"Neni rozdil, pokud se pouziti zavorky nebo hraante zavorky pro vzorek "
"posloupnosti (tj. (...) vs [...])."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:975
msgid ""
"A single pattern enclosed in parentheses without a trailing comma (e.g. ``(3"
" | 4)``) is a :ref:`group pattern <group-patterns>`. While a single pattern "
"enclosed in square brackets (e.g. ``[3 | 4]``) is still a sequence pattern."
msgstr ""
"Jeden vzorek zabalit v zavorkach bez zacinajici carky (napр. (3 | 4)) je "
":ref:`skupinovy vzorek <group-patterns>`. Zatmco jeden vzorek zabalit v "
"hranatnch zavorkach (napр. [3 | 4]) je stale vzorek posloupnosti."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:980
msgid ""
"At most one star subpattern may be in a sequence pattern.  The star "
"subpattern may occur in any position. If no star subpattern is present, the "
"sequence pattern is a fixed-length sequence pattern; otherwise it is a "
"variable-length sequence pattern."
msgstr ""
"V vzorcch posloupnosti ma byt nejvse jeden hvezdickovy podvzorek. "
"Hvezdickovy podvzorek se muze objevit na jakemkoli miste. Pokud neni "
"hvezdickovy podvzorek pritomen, je vzorek posloupnosti vzorek posloupnosti s"
" fixni delkou; v opacnem pripade je to vzorek posloupnosti s variabilni "
"delkou."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:985
msgid ""
"The following is the logical flow for matching a sequence pattern against a "
"subject value:"
msgstr ""
"Následující je logický tok pro matchování vzorců posloupnosti proti hodnotě "
"subjektu:"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:988
msgid ""
"If the subject value is not a sequence [#]_, the sequence pattern fails."
msgstr ""
"Pokud hodnota subjektu neni posloupnost [#]_, vzorek posloupnosti selha."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:991
msgid ""
"If the subject value is an instance of ``str``, ``bytes`` or ``bytearray`` "
"the sequence pattern fails."
msgstr ""
"Pokud je hodnota subjektu instanci str, bytes nebo bytearray, vzorek "
"posloupnosti selha."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:994
msgid ""
"The subsequent steps depend on whether the sequence pattern is fixed or "
"variable-length."
msgstr ""
"Nasledujici kroky zavisi na tom, zda je vzorek posloupnosti fixni nebo "
"variabilni delky."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:997
msgid "If the sequence pattern is fixed-length:"
msgstr "Pokud je vzorek posloupnosti fixni delky:"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:999
msgid ""
"If the length of the subject sequence is not equal to the number of "
"subpatterns, the sequence pattern fails"
msgstr ""
"Pokud se delka posloupnosti subjektu nerovna poctu podvzorc, vzorek "
"posloupnosti selha"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1002
msgid ""
"Subpatterns in the sequence pattern are matched to their corresponding items"
" in the subject sequence from left to right.  Matching stops as soon as a "
"subpattern fails.  If all subpatterns succeed in matching their "
"corresponding item, the sequence pattern succeeds."
msgstr ""
"Podvzorce v vzorc posloupnosti jsou matchovany na jejich odpovidajici prvky "
"v posloupnosti subjektu zleva doprava. Matchovani se zastavi jakmile "
"podvzorek selha. Pokud jsou vsechny podvzorce uspesne matchovany s jejich "
"odpovidajicim prvkem, vzorek posloupnosti je uspesny."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1007
msgid "Otherwise, if the sequence pattern is variable-length:"
msgstr "Jinak, pokud je vzorek posloupnosti variabilni delky:"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1009
msgid ""
"If the length of the subject sequence is less than the number of non-star "
"subpatterns, the sequence pattern fails."
msgstr ""
"Pokud je delka posloupnosti subjektu mensi nez pocet non-star podvzorc, "
"vzorek posloupnosti selha."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1012
msgid ""
"The leading non-star subpatterns are matched to their corresponding items as"
" for fixed-length sequences."
msgstr ""
"Vedouci non-star podvzorce jsou matchovany na jejich odpovidajici prvky jako"
" pro posloupnosti fixni delky."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1015
msgid ""
"If the previous step succeeds, the star subpattern matches a list formed of "
"the remaining subject items, excluding the remaining items corresponding to "
"non-star subpatterns following the star subpattern."
msgstr ""
"Pokud je predchozi krok uspesny, hvezdickovy podvzorek matchuje seznam "
"formovany z zbyvajicch prvku subjektu, vyjmeme zbyvajici prvky odpovidajici "
"non-star podvzorc nasledujici hvezdickovy podvzorek."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1019
msgid ""
"Remaining non-star subpatterns are matched to their corresponding subject "
"items, as for a fixed-length sequence."
msgstr ""
"Zbyvajici non-star podvzorce jsou matchovany na jejich odpovidajici prvky "
"subjektu, jako pro posloupnost fixni delky."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1022
msgid ""
"The length of the subject sequence is obtained via :func:`len` (i.e. via the"
" :meth:`~object.__len__` protocol). This length may be cached by the "
"interpreter in a similar manner as :ref:`value patterns <value-patterns>`."
msgstr ""
"Delka posloupnosti subjektu je ziskana pomoci :func:`len` (tj. pomoci "
":meth:`~object.__len__` protokolu). Tato delka muze byt cached interpretrem "
"podobnym zpusobem jako :ref:`value patterns <value-patterns>`."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1028
msgid ""
"In simple terms ``[P1, P2, P3,`` ... ``, P<N>]`` matches only if all the "
"following happens:"
msgstr ""
"Jednoduchy mi slovy [P1, P2, P3, ... , P<N>] matchuje pouze pokud se vse "
"nasledujici deje:"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1031
msgid "check ``<subject>`` is a sequence"
msgstr "kontrola <subject> je posloupnost"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1032
msgid "``len(subject) == <N>``"
msgstr "len(subject) == <N>"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1033
msgid ""
"``P1`` matches ``<subject>[0]`` (note that this match can also bind names)"
msgstr ""
"P1 matchuje <subject>[0] (poznamka, ze tato shoda muze take vazat jmena)"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1034
msgid ""
"``P2`` matches ``<subject>[1]`` (note that this match can also bind names)"
msgstr ""
"P2 matchuje <subject>[1] (poznamka, ze tato shoda muze take vazat jmena)"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1035
msgid "... and so on for the corresponding pattern/element."
msgstr "... a tak dale pro odpovidajici vzorek/prvek."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1040
msgid "Mapping Patterns"
msgstr "Vzorek mapovani"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1042
msgid ""
"A mapping pattern contains one or more key-value patterns.  The syntax is "
"similar to the construction of a dictionary. Syntax:"
msgstr ""
"Vzorek mapovani obsahuje jeden nebo vice klicovych dvojic. Syntax je podobna"
" konstrukci slovniku. Syntax:"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1053
msgid ""
"At most one double star pattern may be in a mapping pattern.  The double "
"star pattern must be the last subpattern in the mapping pattern."
msgstr ""
"V vzorc mapovani muze byt nejvice jeden double star vzorek. Double star "
"vzorek musi byt posledni podvzorek v vzorc mapovani."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1056
msgid ""
"Duplicate keys in mapping patterns are disallowed. Duplicate literal keys "
"will raise a :exc:`SyntaxError`. Two keys that otherwise have the same value"
" will raise a :exc:`ValueError` at runtime."
msgstr ""
"Duplikatni klice v vzorcch mapovani nejsou povoleny. Duplikatni literalni "
"klice vyvolaji :exc:`SyntaxError`. Dva klice, ktere maji jinou hodnotu, "
"vyvolaji :exc:`ValueError` za behu."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1060
msgid ""
"The following is the logical flow for matching a mapping pattern against a "
"subject value:"
msgstr ""
"Nasledujici je logicky tok pro matchovani vzorc mapovani proti hodnote "
"subjektu:"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1063
msgid "If the subject value is not a mapping [#]_,the mapping pattern fails."
msgstr "Pokud hodnota subjektu neni mapovani [#]_, vzorek mapovani selha."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1065
msgid ""
"If every key given in the mapping pattern is present in the subject mapping,"
" and the pattern for each key matches the corresponding item of the subject "
"mapping, the mapping pattern succeeds."
msgstr ""
"Pokud je kazddy klic dany v vzorc mapovani pritomen v mapovani subjektu a "
"vzorek pro kazddy klic matchuje odpovidajici prvek mapovani subjektu, vzorek"
" mapovani je uspesny."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1069
msgid ""
"If duplicate keys are detected in the mapping pattern, the pattern is "
"considered invalid. A :exc:`SyntaxError` is raised for duplicate literal "
"values; or a :exc:`ValueError` for named keys of the same value."
msgstr ""
"Pokud jsou deteklovany duplikatni klice v vzorc mapovani, je vzorek "
"povazovan za neplatny. :exc:`SyntaxError` je vyvolana pro duplikatni "
"literalni hodnoty; nebo :exc:`ValueError` pro pojmenovane klice stejne "
"hodnoty."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1073
msgid ""
"Key-value pairs are matched using the two-argument form of the mapping "
"subject's ``get()`` method.  Matched key-value pairs must already be present"
" in the mapping, and not created on-the-fly via :meth:`~object.__missing__` "
"or :meth:`~object.__getitem__`."
msgstr ""
"Klicove dvojice jsou matchovany pouzitim dvou-argumentove formy metody "
"``get()`` mapovani subjektu. Matchovane klicove dvojice musi jiz byt "
"pritomny v mapovani a nesmejí byt vytvoreny za letu pomoci "
":meth:`~object.__missing__` nebo :meth:`~object.__getitem__`."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1078
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"In simple terms ``{KEY1: P1, KEY2: P2, ... }`` matches only if all the "
"following happens:"
msgstr ""
"Jednoduchy mi slovy {KEY1: P1, KEY2: P2, ... } matchuje pouze pokud se vse "
"nasledujici deje:"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1081
msgid "check ``<subject>`` is a mapping"
msgstr "kontrola <subject> je mapovani"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1082
msgid "``KEY1 in <subject>``"
msgstr "KEY1 in <subject>"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1083
msgid "``P1`` matches ``<subject>[KEY1]``"
msgstr "P1 matchuje <subject>[KEY1]"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1084
msgid "... and so on for the corresponding KEY/pattern pair."
msgstr "... a tak dale pro odpovidajici KEY/vzorek dvojici."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1090
msgid "Class Patterns"
msgstr "Vzorek tridy"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1092
msgid ""
"A class pattern represents a class and its positional and keyword arguments "
"(if any).  Syntax:"
msgstr ""
"Vzorek tridy reprezentuje tridu a jeji pozitonalni a klicova argumenty "
"(pokud jsou). Syntax:"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1103
msgid "The same keyword should not be repeated in class patterns."
msgstr "Stejny klicovy slovy by se nemel opakovat ve vzorcch trid."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1105
msgid ""
"The following is the logical flow for matching a class pattern against a "
"subject value:"
msgstr ""
"Nasledujici je logicky tok pro matchovani vzorc tridy proti hodnote "
"subjektu:"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1108
msgid ""
"If ``name_or_attr`` is not an instance of the builtin :class:`type` , raise "
":exc:`TypeError`."
msgstr ""
"Pokud name_or_attr neni instanci vestavene :class:`type`, vyvolej "
":exc:`TypeError`."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1111
msgid ""
"If the subject value is not an instance of ``name_or_attr`` (tested via "
":func:`isinstance`), the class pattern fails."
msgstr ""
"Pokud hodnota subjektu neni instanci name_or_attr (testovano pomoci "
":func:`isinstance`), vzorek tridy selha."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1114
msgid ""
"If no pattern arguments are present, the pattern succeeds.  Otherwise, the "
"subsequent steps depend on whether keyword or positional argument patterns "
"are present."
msgstr ""
"Pokud nejsou pritomny zadne argumenty vzorc, vzorek je uspesny. Jinak, "
"nasledujici kroky zavisi na tom, zda jsou pritomny klicove nebo pozitonalni "
"argumenty vzorc."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1118
msgid ""
"For a number of built-in types (specified below), a single positional "
"subpattern is accepted which will match the entire subject; for these types "
"keyword patterns also work as for other types."
msgstr ""
"Pro pocet vestavennych typu (specifikovany nize), je prijet jeden "
"pozitonalni podvzorek, ktery matchuje cely subjekt; pro tyto typy klicove "
"vzorek take pracuji jako pro jine typy."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1122
msgid ""
"If only keyword patterns are present, they are processed as follows, one by "
"one:"
msgstr ""
"Pokud jsou pritomny pouze klicove vzorc, jsou zpracovany nasledovne, jeden "
"po druh:"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1125
msgid "The keyword is looked up as an attribute on the subject."
msgstr "Klic se vyhledava jako atribut na subjektu."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1127
msgid ""
"If this raises an exception other than :exc:`AttributeError`, the exception "
"bubbles up."
msgstr ""
"Pokud to vyvola vyjimku jinou nez :exc:`AttributeError`, vyjimka se siri."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1130
msgid "If this raises :exc:`AttributeError`, the class pattern has failed."
msgstr "Pokud to vyvola :exc:`AttributeError`, vzorek tridy selha."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1132
msgid ""
"Else, the subpattern associated with the keyword pattern is matched against "
"the subject's attribute value.  If this fails, the class pattern fails; if "
"this succeeds, the match proceeds to the next keyword."
msgstr ""
"Jinak, podvzorek spojeny s klicovym vzorcem je matchovan proti hodnote "
"atributu subjektu. Pokud se nepovede, vzorek tridy selha; pokud se povede, "
"shoda pokracuje k dalsimu klici."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1137
msgid "If all keyword patterns succeed, the class pattern succeeds."
msgstr "Pokud jsou vsechny klicove vzorc uspesne, vzorek tridy je uspesny."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1139
msgid ""
"If any positional patterns are present, they are converted to keyword "
"patterns using the :data:`~object.__match_args__` attribute on the class "
"``name_or_attr`` before matching:"
msgstr ""
"Pokud jsou pritomny jakekoli pozitonalni vzorc, jsou konvertovany na klicove"
" vzorc pouzitim atributu :data:`~object.__match_args__` na tride "
"name_or_attr pred matchovanim:"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1143
msgid "The equivalent of ``getattr(cls, \"__match_args__\", ())`` is called."
msgstr "Ekvivalent ``getattr(cls, \"__match_args__\", ())`` je zavolana."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1145
msgid "If this raises an exception, the exception bubbles up."
msgstr "Pokud to vyvola vyjimku, vyjimka se siri."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1147
msgid ""
"If the returned value is not a tuple, the conversion fails and "
":exc:`TypeError` is raised."
msgstr ""
"Pokud vracena hodnota neni n-tice, konverze se neuda a :exc:`TypeError` je "
"vyvolana."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1150
msgid ""
"If there are more positional patterns than ``len(cls.__match_args__)``, "
":exc:`TypeError` is raised."
msgstr ""
"Pokud je vice pozitonalnich vzorc nez ``len(cls.__match_args__)``, "
":exc:`TypeError` je vyvolana."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1153
msgid ""
"Otherwise, positional pattern ``i`` is converted to a keyword pattern using "
"``__match_args__[i]`` as the keyword.  ``__match_args__[i]`` must be a "
"string; if not :exc:`TypeError` is raised."
msgstr ""
"Jinak, pozitonalni vzorek i je konvertovan na klicovy vzorek pouzitim "
"``__match_args__[i]`` jako klic. ``__match_args__[i]`` musi byt retezec; "
"pokud ne :exc:`TypeError` je vyvolana."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1157
msgid "If there are duplicate keywords, :exc:`TypeError` is raised."
msgstr "Pokud jsou duplikatni klice, :exc:`TypeError` je vyvolana."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1159
msgid ":ref:`class-pattern-matching`"
msgstr ":ref:`class-pattern-matching`"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1161
msgid ""
"Once all positional patterns have been converted to keyword patterns, the "
"match proceeds as if there were only keyword patterns."
msgstr ""
"Jakmile jsou vsechny pozitonalni vzorc konvertovany na klicove vzorc, shoda "
"pokracuje jako kdyby byly pouze klicove vzorc."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1164
msgid ""
"For the following built-in types the handling of positional subpatterns is "
"different:"
msgstr ""
"Pro nasledujici vestavene typy je zachazeni s pozitonalnimi podvzorci "
"odlisne:"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1167
msgid ":class:`bool`"
msgstr ":class:`bool`"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1168
msgid ":class:`bytearray`"
msgstr ":class:`bytearray`"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1169
msgid ":class:`bytes`"
msgstr ":class:`bytes`"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1170
msgid ":class:`dict`"
msgstr ":class:`dict`"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1171
msgid ":class:`float`"
msgstr ":class:`float`"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1172
msgid ":class:`frozenset`"
msgstr ":class:`frozenset`"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1173
msgid ":class:`int`"
msgstr ":class:`int`"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1174
#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1932
msgid ":class:`list`"
msgstr ":class:`list`"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1175
msgid ":class:`set`"
msgstr ":class:`set`"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1176
msgid ":class:`str`"
msgstr ":class:`str`"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1177
#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1935
msgid ":class:`tuple`"
msgstr ":class:`tuple`"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1179
msgid ""
"These classes accept a single positional argument, and the pattern there is "
"matched against the whole object rather than an attribute. For example "
"``int(0|1)`` matches the value ``0``, but not the value ``0.0``."
msgstr ""
"Tyto tridy prijimaji jeden pozitonalni argument a vzorek tam je matchovan "
"proti celem objektu spise nez proti atributu. Napr int(0|1) matchuje hodnotu"
" 0, ale ne hodnotu 0.0."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1183
msgid ""
"In simple terms ``CLS(P1, attr=P2)`` matches only if the following happens:"
msgstr ""
"Jednoduchy mi slovy CLS(P1, attr=P2) matchuje pouze pokud se nasledujici "
"deje:"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1185
msgid "``isinstance(<subject>, CLS)``"
msgstr "isinstance(<subject>, CLS)"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1186
msgid "convert ``P1`` to a keyword pattern using ``CLS.__match_args__``"
msgstr "konvertuj P1 na klicovy vzorek pouzitim CLS.__match_args__"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1187
msgid "For each keyword argument ``attr=P2``:"
msgstr "Pro kazddy klicovy argument attr=P2:"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1189
msgid "``hasattr(<subject>, \"attr\")``"
msgstr "hasattr(<subject>, \"attr\")"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1190
msgid "``P2`` matches ``<subject>.attr``"
msgstr "P2 matchuje <subject>.attr"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1192
msgid "... and so on for the corresponding keyword argument/pattern pair."
msgstr "... a tak dale pro odpovidajici klicovy argument/vzorek dvojici."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1207
msgid "Function definitions"
msgstr "Definice funkci"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1222
msgid ""
"A function definition defines a user-defined function object (see section "
":ref:`types`):"
msgstr ""
"Definice funkce definuje uzivatelskou funkci objekt (viz sekce "
":ref:`types`):"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1244
msgid ""
"A function definition is an executable statement.  Its execution binds the "
"function name in the current local namespace to a function object (a wrapper"
" around the executable code for the function).  This function object "
"contains a reference to the current global namespace as the global namespace"
" to be used when the function is called."
msgstr ""
"Definice funkce je spustitelny prikaz. Jeji provedeni vazani jmeno funkce v "
"aktualni lokalni namespace na funkci objekt (obalu kolem spustitelneho kodu "
"pro funkci). Tento funkci objekt obsahuje odkaz na aktualni globalni "
"namespace jako globalni namespace, ktere se budou pouzivat, kdyz je funkce "
"volana."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1250
msgid ""
"The function definition does not execute the function body; this gets "
"executed only when the function is called. [#]_"
msgstr ""
"Definice funkce neproves telo funkce; toto se vykonava pouze kdyz je funkce "
"volana. [#]_"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1256
msgid ""
"A function definition may be wrapped by one or more :term:`decorator` "
"expressions. Decorator expressions are evaluated when the function is "
"defined, in the scope that contains the function definition.  The result "
"must be a callable, which is invoked with the function object as the only "
"argument. The returned value is bound to the function name instead of the "
"function object.  Multiple decorators are applied in nested fashion. For "
"example, the following code ::"
msgstr ""
"Definice funkce muze byt obalena jednim nebo vice :term:`decorator` vyrazy. "
"Dekorator vyrazy se vyhodnocuji kdyz je funkce definovana, v oboru, ktere "
"obsahuje definici funkce. Vysledek musi byt volatelna, ktera je vyvolana s "
"funkci objektem jako jedine argumentem. Vracena hodnota je vazana na jmeno "
"funkce miste funkci objektu. Vicesobne dekoratory jsou aplikovany vnorenym "
"zpusobem. Napr. nasledujici kod ::"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1263
msgid ""
"@f1(arg)\n"
"@f2\n"
"def func(): pass"
msgstr ""
"@f1(arg)\n"
"@f2\n"
"def func(): pass"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1267
#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1456
msgid "is roughly equivalent to ::"
msgstr "je zhruba ekvivalentni ::"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1269
msgid ""
"def func(): pass\n"
"func = f1(arg)(f2(func))"
msgstr ""
"def func(): pass\n"
"func = f1(arg)(f2(func))"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1272
msgid ""
"except that the original function is not temporarily bound to the name "
"``func``."
msgstr "krome toho, ze puvodni funkce neni docasne vazana na jmeno func."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1274
msgid ""
"Functions may be decorated with any valid :token:`~python-"
"grammar:assignment_expression`. Previously, the grammar was much more "
"restrictive; see :pep:`614` for details."
msgstr ""
"Funkce mohou byt dekorovany jakymkoli platnym :token:`~python-"
"grammar:assignment_expression`. Driv byl vykaz mnohem vice restrikivni; "
"vizte :pep:`614` pro detaily."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1279
msgid ""
"A list of :ref:`type parameters <type-params>` may be given in square "
"brackets between the function's name and the opening parenthesis for its "
"parameter list. This indicates to static type checkers that the function is "
"generic. At runtime, the type parameters can be retrieved from the "
"function's :attr:`~function.__type_params__` attribute. See :ref:`generic-"
"functions` for more."
msgstr ""
"Seznam :ref:`typu parametru <type-params>` muze byt dan v hranatnycch "
"zavorkach mezi jmenem funkce a otviraci zavorkou pro jeji seznam parametru. "
"To indikuje do statickyho kontroly typu, ze funkce je generovana. Pri "
"bezinu, typove parametry mohou byt ziskany z "
":attr:`~function.__type_params__` atributu funkce. Vizte :ref:`generic-"
"functions` pro vice."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1286
#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1475
msgid "Type parameter lists are new in Python 3.12."
msgstr "Seznamy typu parametru jsou nove v Pythonu 3.12."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1294
msgid ""
"When one or more :term:`parameters <parameter>` have the form *parameter* "
"``=`` *expression*, the function is said to have \"default parameter "
"values.\"  For a parameter with a default value, the corresponding "
":term:`argument` may be omitted from a call, in which case the parameter's "
"default value is substituted.  If a parameter has a default value, all "
"following parameters up until the \"``*``\" must also have a default value "
"--- this is a syntactic restriction that is not expressed by the grammar."
msgstr ""
"Kdyz jeden nebo vice :term:`parametru <parameter>` ma formu *parameter* "
"``=`` *expression*, funkce se rekne, ze ma \"vychozi hodnoty parametru\". "
"Pro parametr s vychozi hodnotou, odpovidajici :term:`argument` muze byt "
"vynechan z volani, v cemz pripade se pouzije vychozi hodnota parametru. "
"Pokud ma parametr vychozi hodnotu, vsichni nasledujici parametry az "
"\"``*``\" musi take mit vychozi hodnotu --- toto je syntakticke omezeni, "
"ktere neni vyjadrem gramatikou."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1302
msgid ""
"**Default parameter values are evaluated from left to right when the "
"function definition is executed.** This means that the expression is "
"evaluated once, when the function is defined, and that the same \"pre-"
"computed\" value is used for each call.  This is especially important to "
"understand when a default parameter value is a mutable object, such as a "
"list or a dictionary: if the function modifies the object (e.g. by appending"
" an item to a list), the default parameter value is in effect modified.  "
"This is generally not what was intended.  A way around this is to use "
"``None`` as the default, and explicitly test for it in the body of the "
"function, e.g.::"
msgstr ""
"**Vychozi hodnoty parametru jsou vyhodnocovany zleva doprava, kdyz je "
"definice funkce vykonana.** To znamena, ze vyraz je vyhodnocen jednou, kdyz "
"je funkce definovana a ze stejna \"pred-vypocitana\" hodnota se pouziva pro "
"kazdde volani. Toto je zvlaste dulezite pochopit, kdyz je vychozi hodnota "
"parametru menitelny objekt, jako je seznam nebo slovnik: pokud funkce "
"modifikuje objekt (napr. pripojim prvek do seznamu), vychozi hodnota "
"parametru je v podstate modifikovana. Toto obecne neni to, co bylo "
"zamislenho. Zpusob, jak se kolem toho dostat je pouziti ``None`` jako "
"vychozi a explicitne to otestovat v tele funkce, napr.::"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1312
msgid ""
"def whats_on_the_telly(penguin=None):\n"
"    if penguin is None:\n"
"        penguin = []\n"
"    penguin.append(\"property of the zoo\")\n"
"    return penguin"
msgstr ""
"def whats_on_the_telly(penguin=None):\n"
"    if penguin is None:\n"
"        penguin = []\n"
"    penguin.append(\"property of the zoo\")\n"
"    return penguin"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1323
msgid ""
"Function call semantics are described in more detail in section "
":ref:`calls`. A function call always assigns values to all parameters "
"mentioned in the parameter list, either from positional arguments, from "
"keyword arguments, or from default values.  If the form \"``*identifier``\" "
"is present, it is initialized to a tuple receiving any excess positional "
"parameters, defaulting to the empty tuple. If the form \"``**identifier``\" "
"is present, it is initialized to a new ordered mapping receiving any excess "
"keyword arguments, defaulting to a new empty mapping of the same type.  "
"Parameters after \"``*``\" or \"``*identifier``\" are keyword-only "
"parameters and may only be passed by keyword arguments.  Parameters before "
"\"``/``\" are positional-only parameters and may only be passed by "
"positional arguments."
msgstr ""
"Semantika volani funkce je podrobneji popsana v sekci :ref:`calls`. Volani "
"funkce vzdy priradi hodnoty vsem parametrum vyjmenovanym v seznamu "
"parametru, bud z pozitonalnich argumentu, z klicovych argumentu nebo z "
"vychozich hodnot. Pokud je pritomna forma \"``*identifier``\", je "
"inicializovana na tuple prijimajici jakekoli vistecne pozitonalni parametry,"
" vychozi prazdne tuple. Pokud je pritomna forma \"``**identifier``\", je "
"inicializovana na novy usporadany mapping prijimajici jakekoli vistecne "
"klicove argumenty, vychozi prazdny mapping stejneho typu. Parametry za "
"\"``*``\" nebo \"``*identifier``\" jsou pouze klicove parametry a mohou byt "
"predan pouze klicovymi argumenty. Parametry pred \"``/``\" jsou pouze "
"pozitonalne parametry a mohou byt predan pouze pozitonalnymi argumenty."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1335
msgid ""
"The ``/`` function parameter syntax may be used to indicate positional-only "
"parameters. See :pep:`570` for details."
msgstr ""
"Syntaxe ``/`` parametru funkce muze byt pouzita k indikaci pouze "
"pozitonalnich parametru. Vizte :pep:`570` pro detaily."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1344
msgid ""
"Parameters may have an :term:`annotation <function annotation>` of the form "
"\"``: expression``\" following the parameter name.  Any parameter may have "
"an annotation, even those of the form ``*identifier`` or ``**identifier``. "
"(As a special case, parameters of the form ``*identifier`` may have an "
"annotation \"``: *expression``\".) Functions may have \"return\" annotation "
"of the form \"``-> expression``\" after the parameter list.  These "
"annotations can be any valid Python expression.  The presence of annotations"
" does not change the semantics of a function. See :ref:`annotations` for "
"more information on annotations."
msgstr ""
"Parametry mohou mit :term:`anotace <function annotation>` formy \"``: "
"expression``\" nasledujici jmeno parametru. Jakykoli parametr muze mit "
"anotaci, dokonce i ty formy ``*identifier`` nebo ``**identifier``. (Jako "
"specialni pripad, parametry formy ``*identifier`` mohou mit anotaci \"``: "
"*expression``\".) Funkce mohou mit \"return\" anotaci formy \"``-> "
"expression``\" za seznamem parametru. Tyto anotace mohou byt jakakoli platna"
" Python vyrazu. Pritomnost anotaci nemeni semantiku funkce. Vizte "
":ref:`annotations` pro vice informaci o anotacich."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1352
msgid ""
"Parameters of the form \"``*identifier``\" may have an annotation \"``: "
"*expression``\". See :pep:`646`."
msgstr ""
"Parametry formy \"``*identifier``\" mohou mit anotaci \"``: *expression``\"."
" Vizte :pep:`646`."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1358
msgid ""
"It is also possible to create anonymous functions (functions not bound to a "
"name), for immediate use in expressions.  This uses lambda expressions, "
"described in section :ref:`lambda`.  Note that the lambda expression is "
"merely a shorthand for a simplified function definition; a function defined "
"in a \":keyword:`def`\" statement can be passed around or assigned to "
"another name just like a function defined by a lambda expression.  The "
"\":keyword:`!def`\" form is actually more powerful since it allows the "
"execution of multiple statements and annotations."
msgstr ""
"Je mozne take vytvorit anonymni funkce (funkce nevazane na jmeno), pro "
"okamzite pouziti ve vyrazech. Toto pouziva lambda vyrazy, popsane v sekci "
":ref:`lambda`. Poznamka, ze lambda vyraz je pouze zkratkou pro zjednodusou "
"definici funkce; funkce definovana v \":keyword:`def`\" prikazu muze byt "
"cestnena nebo priruzena jineho jmena stejne jako funkce definovana lambda "
"vyrazu. \":keyword:`!def`\" forma je ve skutecnosti mocnejsi, nebot umoznuje"
" provedeni vice prikazu a anotaci."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1366
msgid ""
"**Programmer's note:** Functions are first-class objects.  A \"``def``\" "
"statement executed inside a function definition defines a local function "
"that can be returned or passed around.  Free variables used in the nested "
"function can access the local variables of the function containing the def."
"  See section :ref:`naming` for details."
msgstr ""
"**Poznamka programatora:** Funkce jsou prvni-tridy objekty. \"``def``\" "
"prikaz vykonal uvnitr definice funkce definuje lokalni funkci, ktera muze "
"byt vracena nebo poslan okolo. Volne promenne pouzite v vnorene funkci mohou"
" pristoupit k lokalnim promennym funkce obsahujici def. Vizte sekce "
":ref:`naming` pro detaily."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1374
msgid ":pep:`3107` - Function Annotations"
msgstr ":pep:`3107` - Anotace funkce"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1375
msgid "The original specification for function annotations."
msgstr "Puvodni specifikace pro anotace funkce."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1377
msgid ":pep:`484` - Type Hints"
msgstr ":pep:`484` - Tipy typu"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1378
msgid "Definition of a standard meaning for annotations: type hints."
msgstr "Definice standardniho vyznamuu pro anotace: tipy typu."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1380
msgid ":pep:`526` - Syntax for Variable Annotations"
msgstr ":pep:`526` - Syntaxe pro anotace promenne"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1381
msgid ""
"Ability to type hint variable declarations, including class variables and "
"instance variables."
msgstr ""
"Schopnost cislit promenne deklarace, vcetne tridnich promennych a "
"instancnich promennych."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1384
msgid ":pep:`563` - Postponed Evaluation of Annotations"
msgstr ":pep:`563` - Odlozene vyhodnoceni anotaci"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1385
msgid ""
"Support for forward references within annotations by preserving annotations "
"in a string form at runtime instead of eager evaluation."
msgstr ""
"Podpora pro vperedi odkazy v anotacich zachovanim anotaci v retezci formu za"
" behu miste pospiechaneho vyhodnoceni."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1388
msgid ":pep:`318` - Decorators for Functions and Methods"
msgstr ":pep:`318` - Dekoratory pro funkce a metody"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1389
msgid ""
"Function and method decorators were introduced. Class decorators were "
"introduced in :pep:`3129`."
msgstr ""
"Dekoratory funkci a metod byly zavedeny. Dekoratory trid byly zavedeny v "
":pep:`3129`."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1395
msgid "Class definitions"
msgstr "Definice trid"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1410
msgid "A class definition defines a class object (see section :ref:`types`):"
msgstr "Definice tridy definuje objekt tridy (viz sekce :ref:`types`):"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1417
msgid ""
"A class definition is an executable statement.  The inheritance list usually"
" gives a list of base classes (see :ref:`metaclasses` for more advanced "
"uses), so each item in the list should evaluate to a class object which "
"allows subclassing.  Classes without an inheritance list inherit, by "
"default, from the base class :class:`object`; hence, ::"
msgstr ""
"Definice tridy je spustitelny prikaz. Seznam dedicnosti obykle da seznam "
"zakladnich trid (vizte :ref:`metaclasses` pro pokrocilnejsi pouziti), tak ze"
" kazda položkov v seznamu by mela vyhodnotit objekt tridy, ktery umoznuje "
"podtridu. Tridy bez seznamu dedicnosti dedicnost, ve vychozim stavu, ze "
"zakladni tridy :class:`object`; odtud, ::"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1423
msgid ""
"class Foo:\n"
"    pass"
msgstr ""
"class Foo:\n"
"    pass"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1426
msgid "is equivalent to ::"
msgstr "je ekvivalentni ::"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1428
msgid ""
"class Foo(object):\n"
"    pass"
msgstr ""
"class Foo(object):\n"
"    pass"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1431
msgid ""
"The class's suite is then executed in a new execution frame (see "
":ref:`naming`), using a newly created local namespace and the original "
"global namespace. (Usually, the suite contains mostly function definitions.)"
"  When the class's suite finishes execution, its execution frame is "
"discarded but its local namespace is saved. [#]_ A class object is then "
"created using the inheritance list for the base classes and the saved local "
"namespace for the attribute dictionary.  The class name is bound to this "
"class object in the original local namespace."
msgstr ""
"Suite tridy je pak vykonana v novem vy|konavacim rame (vizte :ref:`naming`),"
" pouzivajic nove vytvoreny lokalni namespace a puvodni globalni namespace. "
"(Obvykle, suite obsahuje prevazne definice funkci.) Kdyz provedeni suite "
"tridy skonci, jej|i provadeci ram je vyhozen ale jej|i lokalni namespace je "
"ulozena. [#]_ Objekt tridy je pak vytvoren pouzitim seznamu dedicnosti pro "
"zakladni tridy a ulozenym lokalnim namespace pro slovnik atributu. Jmeno "
"tridy je vazano k tomuto objektu tridy v puvodnim lokalnim namespace."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1440
msgid ""
"The order in which attributes are defined in the class body is preserved in "
"the new class's :attr:`~type.__dict__`.  Note that this is reliable only "
"right after the class is created and only for classes that were defined "
"using the definition syntax."
msgstr ""
"Poradi, ve kterem jsou atributy definovany v tele tridy je zachovano v "
":attr:`~type.__dict__` nove tridy. Poznamka, ze to je spolehlive pouze hned "
"po vytvoreni tridy a pouze pro tridy, ktere byly definovany pouzitim "
"definice syntaxe."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1445
msgid ""
"Class creation can be customized heavily using :ref:`metaclasses "
"<metaclasses>`."
msgstr ""
"Vytvoreni tridy muze byt silne customize pouzitim :ref:`metaclasses "
"<metaclasses>`."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1450
msgid "Classes can also be decorated: just like when decorating functions, ::"
msgstr ""
"Tridy mohou take byt dekorovany: stejne jako kdyz dekorujete funkce, ::"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1452
msgid ""
"@f1(arg)\n"
"@f2\n"
"class Foo: pass"
msgstr ""
"@f1(arg)\n"
"@f2\n"
"class Foo: pass"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1458
msgid ""
"class Foo: pass\n"
"Foo = f1(arg)(f2(Foo))"
msgstr ""
"class Foo: pass\n"
"Foo = f1(arg)(f2(Foo))"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1461
msgid ""
"The evaluation rules for the decorator expressions are the same as for "
"function decorators.  The result is then bound to the class name."
msgstr ""
"Vyhodnocovaci pravidla pro dekorator vyrazy jsou stejne jako pro dekoratory "
"funkci. Vysledek je pak vazany na jmeno tridy."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1464
msgid ""
"Classes may be decorated with any valid :token:`~python-"
"grammar:assignment_expression`. Previously, the grammar was much more "
"restrictive; see :pep:`614` for details."
msgstr ""
"Tridy mohou byt dekorovany s jakymkoli platnym :token:`~python-"
"grammar:assignment_expression`. Driv byla gramatika mnohem vice restrikivni;"
" vizte :pep:`614` pro detaily."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1469
msgid ""
"A list of :ref:`type parameters <type-params>` may be given in square "
"brackets immediately after the class's name. This indicates to static type "
"checkers that the class is generic. At runtime, the type parameters can be "
"retrieved from the class's :attr:`~type.__type_params__` attribute. See "
":ref:`generic-classes` for more."
msgstr ""
"Seznam :ref:`typu parametru <type-params>` muze byt dan v hranatnycch "
"zavorkach bezprostredne po jmene tridy. To indikuje do statickyho typu "
"kontrola, ze trida je generovana. Pri bezinu, typove parametry mohou byt "
"ziskany z :attr:`~type.__type_params__` atributu tridy. Vizte :ref:`generic-"
"classes` pro vice."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1478
msgid ""
"**Programmer's note:** Variables defined in the class definition are class "
"attributes; they are shared by instances.  Instance attributes can be set in"
" a method with ``self.name = value``.  Both class and instance attributes "
"are accessible through the notation \"``self.name``\", and an instance "
"attribute hides a class attribute with the same name when accessed in this "
"way.  Class attributes can be used as defaults for instance attributes, but "
"using mutable values there can lead to unexpected results.  "
":ref:`Descriptors <descriptors>` can be used to create instance variables "
"with different implementation details."
msgstr ""
"**Poznamka programatora:** Promenne definovane v definici tridy jsou "
"atributy trid; jsou sdileny instancemi. Atributy instanci mohou byt "
"nastaveny v metode s ``self.name = value``. Oba atributy trid a instanci "
"jsou dostupne pres zapis \"``self.name``\" a atribut instance skryva atribut"
" tridy se stejnym jmenem, kdyz je pristoupen tymto zpusobem. Atributy trid "
"mohou byt pouzivany jako vychozi instance atributy, ale pouziti menitelnych "
"hodnot tam muze vest na neocekovane vysledky. :ref:`Descriptory "
"<descriptors>` mohou byt pouzivany k vytvoreni instancnich promennych s "
"ruznymi detaily implementace."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1490
msgid ":pep:`3115` - Metaclasses in Python 3000"
msgstr ":pep:`3115` - Metaclasses v Pythonu 3000"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1491
msgid ""
"The proposal that changed the declaration of metaclasses to the current "
"syntax, and the semantics for how classes with metaclasses are constructed."
msgstr ""
"Navrh, ktery zmenil deklaraci metaclasses na soucasnou syntaxi a semantiku "
"toho, jak jsou tridy s metaclasses vytvoreny."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1495
msgid ":pep:`3129` - Class Decorators"
msgstr ":pep:`3129` - Dekoratory trid"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1496
msgid ""
"The proposal that added class decorators.  Function and method decorators "
"were introduced in :pep:`318`."
msgstr ""
"Navrh, ktery pridal dekoratory trid. Dekoratory funkci a metod byly zavedeny"
" v :pep:`318`."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1503
msgid "Coroutines"
msgstr "Korutiny"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1511
msgid "Coroutine function definition"
msgstr "Definice funkce korutiny"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1521
msgid ""
"Execution of Python coroutines can be suspended and resumed at many points "
"(see :term:`coroutine`). :keyword:`await` expressions, :keyword:`async for` "
"and :keyword:`async with` can only be used in the body of a coroutine "
"function."
msgstr ""
"Vykonani Python korutin muze byt pozastaveno a obnoveneo v mnoha bodech "
"(vizte :term:`coroutine`). :keyword:`await` vyrazy, :keyword:`async for` a "
":keyword:`async with` mohou byt pouzivany pouze v tele funkce korutiny."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1525
msgid ""
"Functions defined with ``async def`` syntax are always coroutine functions, "
"even if they do not contain ``await`` or ``async`` keywords."
msgstr ""
"Funkce definovane se ``async def`` syntaxe jsou vzdy funkce korutiny, i kdyz"
" neobsahuji ``await`` nebo ``async`` klicova slova."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1528
msgid ""
"It is a :exc:`SyntaxError` to use a ``yield from`` expression inside the "
"body of a coroutine function."
msgstr ""
"Je :exc:`SyntaxError` pouzit vyraz ``yield from`` uvnitr tela funkce "
"korutiny."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1531
msgid "An example of a coroutine function::"
msgstr "Priklad funkce korutiny::"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1533
msgid ""
"async def func(param1, param2):\n"
"    do_stuff()\n"
"    await some_coroutine()"
msgstr ""
"async def func(param1, param2):\n"
"    do_stuff()\n"
"    await some_coroutine()"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1537
msgid ""
"``await`` and ``async`` are now keywords; previously they were only treated "
"as such inside the body of a coroutine function."
msgstr ""
"``await`` a ``async`` jsou nynni klicova slova; driv byla pouze zachazena "
"jako takova uvnitr tela funkce korutiny."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1545
msgid "The :keyword:`!async for` statement"
msgstr "Příkaz :keyword:`!async for`"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1550
msgid ""
"An :term:`asynchronous iterable` provides an ``__aiter__`` method that "
"directly returns an :term:`asynchronous iterator`, which can call "
"asynchronous code in its ``__anext__`` method."
msgstr ""
"Asynchronni iterable poskytuje ``__aiter__`` metodu, ktera primo vraci "
"asynchronni iterator, ktery muze volat asynchronni kod v jeho ``__anext__`` "
"metode."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1554
msgid ""
"The ``async for`` statement allows convenient iteration over asynchronous "
"iterables."
msgstr ""
"Příkaz ``async for`` umoznuje pohodlnou iteraci pres asynchronni iterables."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1559
msgid ""
"async for TARGET in ITER:\n"
"    SUITE\n"
"else:\n"
"    SUITE2"
msgstr ""
"async for TARGET in ITER:\n"
"    SUITE\n"
"else:\n"
"    SUITE2"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1564
msgid "Is semantically equivalent to::"
msgstr "Je semanticky ekvivalentni::"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1566
msgid ""
"iter = (ITER)\n"
"iter = type(iter).__aiter__(iter)\n"
"running = True\n"
"\n"
"while running:\n"
"    try:\n"
"        TARGET = await type(iter).__anext__(iter)\n"
"    except StopAsyncIteration:\n"
"        running = False\n"
"    else:\n"
"        SUITE\n"
"else:\n"
"    SUITE2"
msgstr ""
"iter = (ITER)\n"
"iter = type(iter).__aiter__(iter)\n"
"running = True\n"
"\n"
"while running:\n"
"    try:\n"
"        TARGET = await type(iter).__anext__(iter)\n"
"    except StopAsyncIteration:\n"
"        running = False\n"
"    else:\n"
"        SUITE\n"
"else:\n"
"    SUITE2"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1580
msgid ""
"See also :meth:`~object.__aiter__` and :meth:`~object.__anext__` for "
"details."
msgstr ""
"Viz také :meth:`~object.__aiter__` a :meth:`~object.__anext__` pro "
"podrobnosti."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1582
msgid ""
"It is a :exc:`SyntaxError` to use an ``async for`` statement outside the "
"body of a coroutine function."
msgstr ""
"Použití příkazu ``async for`` mimo tělo funkce korutiny je "
":exc:`SyntaxError`."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1590
msgid "The :keyword:`!async with` statement"
msgstr "Příkaz :keyword:`!async with`"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1595
msgid ""
"An :term:`asynchronous context manager` is a :term:`context manager` that is"
" able to suspend execution in its *enter* and *exit* methods."
msgstr ""
"Asynchronní správce kontextu je správce kontextu, který je schopen "
"pozastavit provádění v jeho metodách *enter* a *exit*."

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1600
msgid ""
"async with EXPRESSION as TARGET:\n"
"    SUITE"
msgstr ""
"async with VÝRAZ as CÍL:\n"
"    BLOK"

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1605
msgid ""
"manager = (EXPRESSION)\n"
"aenter = type(manager).__aenter__\n"
"aexit = type(manager).__aexit__\n"
"value = await aenter(manager)\n"
"hit_except = False\n"
"\n"
"try:\n"
"    TARGET = value\n"
"    SUITE\n"
"except:\n"
"    hit_except = True\n"
"    if not await aexit(manager, *sys.exc_info()):\n"
"        raise\n"
"finally:\n"
"    if not hit_except:\n"
"        await aexit(manager, None, None, None)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1622
msgid ""
"See also :meth:`~object.__aenter__` and :meth:`~object.__aexit__` for "
"details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1624
msgid ""
"It is a :exc:`SyntaxError` to use an ``async with`` statement outside the "
"body of a coroutine function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1629
msgid ":pep:`492` - Coroutines with async and await syntax"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1630
msgid ""
"The proposal that made coroutines a proper standalone concept in Python, and"
" added supporting syntax."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1636
msgid "Type parameter lists"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1640
msgid "Support for default values was added (see :pep:`696`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1653
msgid ""
":ref:`Functions <def>` (including :ref:`coroutines <async def>`), "
":ref:`classes <class>` and :ref:`type aliases <type>` may contain a type "
"parameter list::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1657
msgid ""
"def max[T](args: list[T]) -> T:\n"
"    ...\n"
"\n"
"async def amax[T](args: list[T]) -> T:\n"
"    ...\n"
"\n"
"class Bag[T]:\n"
"    def __iter__(self) -> Iterator[T]:\n"
"        ...\n"
"\n"
"    def add(self, arg: T) -> None:\n"
"        ...\n"
"\n"
"type ListOrSet[T] = list[T] | set[T]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1672
msgid ""
"Semantically, this indicates that the function, class, or type alias is "
"generic over a type variable. This information is primarily used by static "
"type checkers, and at runtime, generic objects behave much like their non-"
"generic counterparts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1677
msgid ""
"Type parameters are declared in square brackets (``[]``) immediately after "
"the name of the function, class, or type alias. The type parameters are "
"accessible within the scope of the generic object, but not elsewhere. Thus, "
"after a declaration ``def func[T](): pass``, the name ``T`` is not available"
" in the module scope. Below, the semantics of generic objects are described "
"with more precision. The scope of type parameters is modeled with a special "
"function (technically, an :ref:`annotation scope <annotation-scopes>`) that "
"wraps the creation of the generic object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1686
msgid ""
"Generic functions, classes, and type aliases have a "
":attr:`~definition.__type_params__` attribute listing their type parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1689
msgid "Type parameters come in three kinds:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1691
msgid ""
":data:`typing.TypeVar`, introduced by a plain name (e.g., ``T``). "
"Semantically, this represents a single type to a type checker."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1693
msgid ""
":data:`typing.TypeVarTuple`, introduced by a name prefixed with a single "
"asterisk (e.g., ``*Ts``). Semantically, this stands for a tuple of any "
"number of types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1696
msgid ""
":data:`typing.ParamSpec`, introduced by a name prefixed with two asterisks "
"(e.g., ``**P``). Semantically, this stands for the parameters of a callable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1699
msgid ""
":data:`typing.TypeVar` declarations can define *bounds* and *constraints* "
"with a colon (``:``) followed by an expression. A single expression after "
"the colon indicates a bound (e.g. ``T: int``). Semantically, this means that"
" the :data:`!typing.TypeVar` can only represent types that are a subtype of "
"this bound. A parenthesized tuple of expressions after the colon indicates a"
" set of constraints (e.g. ``T: (str, bytes)``). Each member of the tuple "
"should be a type (again, this is not enforced at runtime). Constrained type "
"variables can only take on one of the types in the list of constraints."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1708
msgid ""
"For :data:`!typing.TypeVar`\\ s declared using the type parameter list "
"syntax, the bound and constraints are not evaluated when the generic object "
"is created, but only when the value is explicitly accessed through the "
"attributes ``__bound__`` and ``__constraints__``. To accomplish this, the "
"bounds or constraints are evaluated in a separate :ref:`annotation scope "
"<annotation-scopes>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1714
msgid ""
":data:`typing.TypeVarTuple`\\ s and :data:`typing.ParamSpec`\\ s cannot have"
" bounds or constraints."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1717
msgid ""
"All three flavors of type parameters can also have a *default value*, which "
"is used when the type parameter is not explicitly provided. This is added by"
" appending a single equals sign (``=``) followed by an expression. Like the "
"bounds and constraints of type variables, the default value is not evaluated"
" when the object is created, but only when the type parameter's "
"``__default__`` attribute is accessed. To this end, the default value is "
"evaluated in a separate :ref:`annotation scope <annotation-scopes>`. If no "
"default value is specified for a type parameter, the ``__default__`` "
"attribute is set to the special sentinel object :data:`typing.NoDefault`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1727
msgid ""
"The following example indicates the full set of allowed type parameter "
"declarations::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1729
msgid ""
"def overly_generic[\n"
"   SimpleTypeVar,\n"
"   TypeVarWithDefault = int,\n"
"   TypeVarWithBound: int,\n"
"   TypeVarWithConstraints: (str, bytes),\n"
"   *SimpleTypeVarTuple = (int, float),\n"
"   **SimpleParamSpec = (str, bytearray),\n"
"](\n"
"   a: SimpleTypeVar,\n"
"   b: TypeVarWithDefault,\n"
"   c: TypeVarWithBound,\n"
"   d: Callable[SimpleParamSpec, TypeVarWithConstraints],\n"
"   *e: SimpleTypeVarTuple,\n"
"): ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1747
msgid "Generic functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1749
msgid "Generic functions are declared as follows::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1751
msgid "def func[T](arg: T): ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1753
#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1813
msgid "This syntax is equivalent to::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1755
msgid ""
"annotation-def TYPE_PARAMS_OF_func():\n"
"    T = typing.TypeVar(\"T\")\n"
"    def func(arg: T): ...\n"
"    func.__type_params__ = (T,)\n"
"    return func\n"
"func = TYPE_PARAMS_OF_func()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1762
msgid ""
"Here ``annotation-def`` indicates an :ref:`annotation scope <annotation-"
"scopes>`, which is not actually bound to any name at runtime. (One other "
"liberty is taken in the translation: the syntax does not go through "
"attribute access on the :mod:`typing` module, but creates an instance of "
":data:`typing.TypeVar` directly.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1768
msgid ""
"The annotations of generic functions are evaluated within the annotation "
"scope used for declaring the type parameters, but the function's defaults "
"and decorators are not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1772
msgid ""
"The following example illustrates the scoping rules for these cases, as well"
" as for additional flavors of type parameters::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1775
msgid ""
"@decorator\n"
"def func[T: int, *Ts, **P](*args: *Ts, arg: Callable[P, T] = some_default):\n"
"    ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1779
msgid ""
"Except for the :ref:`lazy evaluation <lazy-evaluation>` of the "
":class:`~typing.TypeVar` bound, this is equivalent to::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1782
msgid ""
"DEFAULT_OF_arg = some_default\n"
"\n"
"annotation-def TYPE_PARAMS_OF_func():\n"
"\n"
"    annotation-def BOUND_OF_T():\n"
"        return int\n"
"    # In reality, BOUND_OF_T() is evaluated only on demand.\n"
"    T = typing.TypeVar(\"T\", bound=BOUND_OF_T())\n"
"\n"
"    Ts = typing.TypeVarTuple(\"Ts\")\n"
"    P = typing.ParamSpec(\"P\")\n"
"\n"
"    def func(*args: *Ts, arg: Callable[P, T] = DEFAULT_OF_arg):\n"
"        ...\n"
"\n"
"    func.__type_params__ = (T, Ts, P)\n"
"    return func\n"
"func = decorator(TYPE_PARAMS_OF_func())"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1801
msgid ""
"The capitalized names like ``DEFAULT_OF_arg`` are not actually bound at "
"runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1807
msgid "Generic classes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1809
msgid "Generic classes are declared as follows::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1811
msgid "class Bag[T]: ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1815
msgid ""
"annotation-def TYPE_PARAMS_OF_Bag():\n"
"    T = typing.TypeVar(\"T\")\n"
"    class Bag(typing.Generic[T]):\n"
"        __type_params__ = (T,)\n"
"        ...\n"
"    return Bag\n"
"Bag = TYPE_PARAMS_OF_Bag()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1823
msgid ""
"Here again ``annotation-def`` (not a real keyword) indicates an "
":ref:`annotation scope <annotation-scopes>`, and the name "
"``TYPE_PARAMS_OF_Bag`` is not actually bound at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1827
msgid ""
"Generic classes implicitly inherit from :data:`typing.Generic`. The base "
"classes and keyword arguments of generic classes are evaluated within the "
"type scope for the type parameters, and decorators are evaluated outside "
"that scope. This is illustrated by this example::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1833
msgid ""
"@decorator\n"
"class Bag(Base[T], arg=T): ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1836
msgid "This is equivalent to::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1838
msgid ""
"annotation-def TYPE_PARAMS_OF_Bag():\n"
"    T = typing.TypeVar(\"T\")\n"
"    class Bag(Base[T], typing.Generic[T], arg=T):\n"
"        __type_params__ = (T,)\n"
"        ...\n"
"    return Bag\n"
"Bag = decorator(TYPE_PARAMS_OF_Bag())"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1849
msgid "Generic type aliases"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1851
msgid ""
"The :keyword:`type` statement can also be used to create a generic type "
"alias::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1853
msgid "type ListOrSet[T] = list[T] | set[T]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1855
msgid ""
"Except for the :ref:`lazy evaluation <lazy-evaluation>` of the value, this "
"is equivalent to::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1858
msgid ""
"annotation-def TYPE_PARAMS_OF_ListOrSet():\n"
"    T = typing.TypeVar(\"T\")\n"
"\n"
"    annotation-def VALUE_OF_ListOrSet():\n"
"        return list[T] | set[T]\n"
"    # In reality, the value is lazily evaluated\n"
"    return typing.TypeAliasType(\"ListOrSet\", VALUE_OF_ListOrSet(), type_params=(T,))\n"
"ListOrSet = TYPE_PARAMS_OF_ListOrSet()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1867
msgid ""
"Here, ``annotation-def`` (not a real keyword) indicates an :ref:`annotation "
"scope <annotation-scopes>`. The capitalized names like "
"``TYPE_PARAMS_OF_ListOrSet`` are not actually bound at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1874
msgid "Annotations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1876
msgid "Annotations are now lazily evaluated by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1879
msgid ""
"Variables and function parameters may carry :term:`annotations "
"<annotation>`, created by adding a colon after the name, followed by an "
"expression::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1882
msgid ""
"x: annotation = 1\n"
"def f(param: annotation): ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1885
msgid "Functions may also carry a return annotation following an arrow::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1887
msgid "def f() -> annotation: ..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1889
msgid ""
"Annotations are conventionally used for :term:`type hints <type hint>`, but "
"this is not enforced by the language, and in general annotations may contain"
" arbitrary expressions. The presence of annotations does not change the "
"runtime semantics of the code, except if some mechanism is used that "
"introspects and uses the annotations (such as :mod:`dataclasses` or "
":func:`functools.singledispatch`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1895
msgid ""
"By default, annotations are lazily evaluated in an :ref:`annotation scope "
"<annotation-scopes>`. This means that they are not evaluated when the code "
"containing the annotation is evaluated. Instead, the interpreter saves "
"information that can be used to evaluate the annotation later if requested. "
"The :mod:`annotationlib` module provides tools for evaluating annotations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1900
msgid ""
"If the :ref:`future statement <future>` ``from __future__ import "
"annotations`` is present, all annotations are instead stored as strings::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1903
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from __future__ import annotations\n"
">>> def f(param: annotation): ...\n"
">>> f.__annotations__\n"
"{'param': 'annotation'}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1908
msgid ""
"This future statement will be deprecated and removed in a future version of "
"Python, but not before Python 3.13 reaches its end of life (see :pep:`749`)."
" When it is used, introspection tools like "
":func:`annotationlib.get_annotations` and :func:`typing.get_type_hints` are "
"less likely to be able to resolve annotations at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1916
msgid "Footnotes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1917
msgid ""
"The exception is propagated to the invocation stack unless there is a "
":keyword:`finally` clause which happens to raise another exception. That new"
" exception causes the old one to be lost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1921
msgid "In pattern matching, a sequence is defined as one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1923
msgid "a class that inherits from :class:`collections.abc.Sequence`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1924
msgid ""
"a Python class that has been registered as :class:`collections.abc.Sequence`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1925
msgid ""
"a builtin class that has its (CPython) :c:macro:`Py_TPFLAGS_SEQUENCE` bit "
"set"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1926
#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1945
msgid "a class that inherits from any of the above"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1928
msgid "The following standard library classes are sequences:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1930
msgid ":class:`array.array`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1931
msgid ":class:`collections.deque`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1933
msgid ":class:`memoryview`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1934
msgid ":class:`range`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1937
msgid ""
"Subject values of type ``str``, ``bytes``, and ``bytearray`` do not match "
"sequence patterns."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1940
msgid "In pattern matching, a mapping is defined as one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1942
msgid "a class that inherits from :class:`collections.abc.Mapping`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1943
msgid ""
"a Python class that has been registered as :class:`collections.abc.Mapping`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1944
msgid ""
"a builtin class that has its (CPython) :c:macro:`Py_TPFLAGS_MAPPING` bit set"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1947
msgid ""
"The standard library classes :class:`dict` and "
":class:`types.MappingProxyType` are mappings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1950
msgid ""
"A string literal appearing as the first statement in the function body is "
"transformed into the function's :attr:`~function.__doc__` attribute and "
"therefore the function's :term:`docstring`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/compound_stmts.rst:1954
msgid ""
"A string literal appearing as the first statement in the class body is "
"transformed into the namespace's :attr:`~type.__doc__` item and therefore "
"the class's :term:`docstring`."
msgstr ""

